# Keeps the Docker build context (and therefore the built image) limited
# to real source. Excluding node_modules matters most: without this, a
# host-installed node_modules (potentially built for a different OS/arch
# than the container) gets copied in AFTER `npm install` already ran
# inside the image, silently overwriting the container's own clean
# install with the host's — a real, machine-dependent build result, not
# a reproducible one.

node_modules/
dist/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
coverage/

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Secrets/certificates, database exports, and generated artifacts
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.dump
*.backup
*.sql.gz
*.log
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.coverage
audit-report.html
